Z||000000||JayUSA77||09-22-2001||01:02 PM||||I was going through ebay (like i usually do everyday) and i came to this 1990 SHO transaxle.  I believe its from the taures if im not mistaken. but im not sure.  Im just curious what do you think the power rating for that transaxle is???? SHO stands for super high ouput so is the transaxle supposed to be super strong and would it work for our car anyways?  Thanks guys<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||summerjim||09-22-2001||03:57 PM||||The tranny is the weakest point in the SHO.<P>The engine is bullet-proof, too bad you can't say the same about the tranny. <P>It's got a cable clutch setup too...||||reg||1
Z||000002||JayUSA77||09-22-2001||04:11 PM||||what do you mean a cable clutch setup???? I currently found out the SHO transaxle is weak but they have rebuild kits that make it super strong which is more than i can say about the getrag.  Will it fit or is there to many modifications needed to make it work???<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||09-22-2001||08:59 PM||||Have you blown a Getrag?  Very few people seem to know where their real upper limit is...<P>If it's not broken, why fix it?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>An Audi 6-speed would be intresting, so would the rear tranny from a C5 vette (both would require longitudinal engines, and the C5 would need a bellhousing I belive.)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||Monkeyman||09-22-2001||09:31 PM||||summerjim--Fieros have a hydraulic clutch setup, not a cable operated one.<P>I think Bob Steiger (Twin Lakes) has either completed or is in the process of building a SHO setup in a Fiero.  You might want to email him to see how things go.  I remember seeing a pic of a finished SHO in a Fiero.  Looked like a <B>really</B> tight fit.||||reg||1
Z||000005||summerjim||09-22-2001||11:18 PM||||Monkeyman, re-read what I posted. I know Fieros have a hydraulic clutch! I was talking about the SHO tranny having the cable clutch.||||reg||1
