Z||000013||artherd||09-25-2001||11:41 PM||||Hey Jay, yeah, the RedLine is just a tranny fluid (but a good, full synthetic special purpose manual transaxle one that I've had good luck with  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>For more on the extra bearings (cool stuff) and input shaft stuff, see <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A>   <P>Some great stuff (like GM part numbers for new input shaft bearings...) at: <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/getraginfo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/getraginfo.htm</A> <P>The diff bearings and MTL fluid I'd definately do, the rest is probally optional (more difficult too)<P>Enjoy!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JayUSA77:<BR><B>Hey artherd isnt the redlind stuff just transaxle fluid and what are external diff bearings, and the input shaft bearing and how much are they and is it worth it.?? Any extra info would be appreciated thanks <BR>J<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
